    "excerpt": "Section 1: Overview. The core idea is to avoid explicitly representing the configuration space and its obstacles (and their boundaries) using various geometric representations, and instead use sampling to guide exploration of the connectivity of the configuration space. Incremental sampling and search involves generating random, non-repeating sample points in the environment to guide a complex search tree that grows continuously, expanding its coverage. As the number of samples increases, we hope to obtain progressively higher-quality shortest paths from the generated tree. This approach is therefore independent of any particular geometric model.",
