    "excerpt": "Recently I was chatting with a highly talented research-oriented friend on my team. He considers his main research area to be information fusion, but he doesn't know much about planning. That day, somehow the conversation drifted to that topic, and he asked me to explain roughly what planning is about. Naturally, I didn't pander to current hot topics like autonomous driving, nor did I try to give an overly official definition. Instead, I tried to convey that planning is essentially \"moving a point from one place to another in space,\" and the fundamental difficulty lies in it being an NP-hard combinatorial optimization problem.",
