    "excerpt": "Parallel computing can theoretically achieve acceleration, but in practice, one must also consider the pressure of computational resource scheduling and memory allocation. Therefore, the more thorough the parallelization or the simpler the addition of threads, the faster the algorithm runs is not necessarily true. We need to match the computation granularity, synchronization cost, and GPU occupancy according to the actual task to select the appropriate CUDA topology and its parameters. At the same time, we should also minimize useless data transfers among all parties, as these consume significant time. The former is reflected in s",
