    "excerpt": "Zhang Xu, male, born in November 1968 in Pingchang, Sichuan, is a professor at Sichuan University, recipient of the National Science Fund for Distinguished Young Scholars, and a selected member of the Chinese Academy of Sciences' 'Hundred Talents Program.' His main research areas are mathematical control theory, along with related partial differential equations and stochastic analysis. He has received the Second Prize of the National Natural Science Award, served as an editorial board member, associate editor, or editor-in-chief for 7 international academic journals, and has been invited to give reports at the International Congress of Mathematicians. In August 2023, he was shortlisted as a valid candidate for the election of academicians of the Chinese Academy of Sciences.",
